    {
      "type": "stage",
      "kicker": "What it is",
      "narration": "Cardiac arrest is the sudden failure of this pump. The heart malfunctions and stops beating effectively, and the fault is electrical. Watch the ventricles. In ventricular fibrillation they no longer contract together: they quiver. Nothing is ejected. Flow through the aorta stops, there is no pulse and no normal breathing, and the patient is unresponsive. From this moment, chest compressions are the only thing moving blood until the heart is restarted.",
      "world": {
        "w": 2600,
        "h": 1200,
