    {
      "type": "stage",
      "kicker": "The rhythms",
      "narration": "The rhythm on the monitor decides what can help. Four rhythms cause cardiac arrest, in two groups. Ventricular fibrillation and pulseless ventricular tachycardia are shockable, so defibrillation is given alongside high-quality chest compressions. Pulseless electrical activity and asystole are not shockable: a shock cannot help, so the treatment is compressions and a systematic search for reversible causes, which later modules cover in detail.",
