    {
      "type": "stage",
      "kicker": "The chain",
      "narration": "Survival depends on a chain of actions. In 2025 the guidelines replaced four separate chains with a single Chain of Survival, for adults and children, in hospital and outside it. It has six links. First, early recognition and emergency activation: someone recognises the arrest and calls for help. Second, high-quality compressions and breaths. Third, defibrillation, without delay. Fourth, advanced resuscitation by the code team. Fifth, care after the arrest. And sixth, recovery and survivorship.",
