    {
      "type": "stage",
      "kicker": "What changed",
      "narration": "If you trained on the 2020 guidelines, you are updating, not relearning. Four separate chains became one. The symbol of the compression link now includes the lungs, because breathing matters, especially in children and in opioid-related arrest. And the terms changed: rescue breaths are now simply breaths, and ventilation means mechanical respiratory support. The rate of 100 to 120 compressions a minute, and the ratio of 30 to 2 for single-rescuer adult resuscitation, still hold.",
