      "type": "stage",
      "kicker": "Recap",
      "narration": "To recap. Cardiac arrest is an electrical failure: the heart stops pumping effectively, and only compressions move blood until it is restarted. Ventricular fibrillation and pulseless ventricular tachycardia are shockable; the other two rhythms are not. And survival depends on one chain of six links, which begins with the nearest person. In the next module: recognising deterioration and arrest, and calling for help.",
